$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a three necked flask, 2-bromoaniline (1.72 g, 10.0 mmol),
(4-fluorophenyl)boronic acid (1.68 g, 12.0 mmol), Na2CO3 (2.65 g, 25.0
mmol) and 50 mL of solvent (toluene/EtOH/H2O = 1:1:1) were added. Then
Pd(PPh3)4 (0.58 g, 0.5 mmol) was added and the mixture was stirred for 6
h at 80 °C under N2. After that, the mixture was cooled to room
temperature, quenched with saturated NH4Cl and extracted with EtOAc. The
organic layer was washed with saturated NaCl and dried over MgSO4. The
mixture was concentrated in vacuum and the residue was purified by flash
column chromatography on silica gel (petroleum ether/ethyl acetate =
20:1). 4'-fluoro-1,1'-biphenyl-2-amine as a brown oil (1.65 g, 88%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 6-(Arylthio)phenanthridines by Copper-Catalyzed Tandem
