$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General reaction procedure of Suzuki coupling
reaction on dichloromethylene derivatives (4, 13 and 26-28) with
arylboronic acids Dichloromethylene derivative (1.0 mmol), aryl-boronic
acid (2.5 mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (30 mg) and PPh3 (20 mg), potassium
carbonate (1.38 g, 10.0 mmol) and benzyltriethyl ammonium chloride (0.5
g, 2.2 mmol) were taken in a mixture of toluene (20 ml) and water (10
ml). The reaction mixture was heated at 110 ºC for 24 h in nitrogen
atmosphere. On completion of reaction the mixture was cooled, and toluene
layer was separated. On removal of toluene the product was purified by
column chromatography using dichloromethane/hexane as eluent. Preparation
of 6-(diphenylmethylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (5) According to general
reaction procedure, 6-(dichloromethylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (4) (0.32 g,
1.0 mmol) and phenylboronic acid (0.26 g, 2.5 mmol) were reacted.
Preparation of 6-(di(naphthalen-2-yl)methylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (8)
According to general reaction procedure,
6-(dichloromethylene)-6H-benzo[cd]pyrene (4) (0.32 g, 1.0 mmol) and
naphthalene-2-boronic acid (0.43 g, 2.5 mmol) were reacted. Product as
yellow solid. Yield: 0.40 g, 79%. Mp: 230 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ:
7.93-7.92 (m, 4H), 7.80-7.66 (m, 10H), 7.56 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H),
7.44-7.41 (m, 4H), 7.23 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.05 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H).
13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz) δ: 145.3, 141.9, 134.1, 133.7, 133.2 132.1,
131.0, 129.3, 129.1, 129.0, 128.4, 128.2, 127.9, 127.6, 127.2, 126.9,
126.2, 125.9, 125.8, 125.4, 125.2. MALDI-TOF MS: calculated for
[C40H24]+: 504.1872, found: 504.1876.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Unsymmetrically Extended Polyfused Aromatics Embedding Coronene and
Perylene Frameworks: Syntheses and Properties
